{
"dur": 77.723,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 4.479,
"text": "When people are frightened, they move their money to the bank they trust most.",
"end": 4.754
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 4.754,
"vo_start": 5.029,
"vo_end": 12.869,
"text": "JPMorgan's deposits went from about seven hundred and forty-one billion dollars at the end of 2007 to more than one trillion by the end of 2008.",
"end": 13.144
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 13.144,
"vo_start": 13.419,
"vo_end": 23.619,
"text": "For 2008, JPMorgan made a profit of five point six billion dollars. Wells Fargo made about two point seven. Citigroup lost about eighteen point seven billion.",
"end": 23.894
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 23.894,
"vo_start": 24.169,
"vo_end": 33.289,
"text": "In October 2008, the Treasury had the biggest banks take government capital. JPMorgan took twenty-five billion dollars, and paid all of it back in 2009.",
"end": 33.564
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 33.564,
"vo_start": 33.839,
"vo_end": 41.719,
"text": "The competition had thinned out. Bear was absorbed, Lehman was gone, Merrill had been sold and Citigroup needed repeated government help.",
"end": 41.994
},
{
"i": 6,
"start": 41.994,
"vo_start": 42.269,
"vo_end": 46.389,
"text": "By 2009, JPMorgan ranked number one in the world for investment banking fees.",
"end": 46.664
},
{
"i": 7,
"start": 46.664,
"vo_start": 46.939,
"vo_end": 51.415,
"text": "In 2010, it earned seventeen point four billion dollars, then a record for the bank.",
"end": 51.69
},
{
"i": 8,
"start": 51.69,
"vo_start": 51.965,
"vo_end": 60.245,
"text": "But the deals came with a bill. Bear and WaMu had sold mortgage bonds before the crash that later went bad, and now JPMorgan owned those problems.",
"end": 60.52
},
{
"i": 9,
"start": 60.52,
"vo_start": 60.795,
"vo_end": 71.583,
"text": "In 2013, JPMorgan agreed to a thirteen billion dollar settlement over mortgage securities sold by itself, Bear Stearns and Washington Mutual, and admitted it had made serious misrepresentations to investors.",
"end": 71.858
},
{
"i": 10,
"start": 71.858,
"vo_start": 72.133,
"vo_end": 76.773,
"text": "Even so, it came out of the crisis bigger and stronger than any of its rivals.",
"end": 77.723
}
],
